. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
.         *Save only subset containing valid values of plh0004 with exactly one
>  child
.         keep if ((plh0004 > 0 & plh0004 != .) & (kidsex02 == -2 & kidsex01 > 
> 0 & !missing(kidsex01)))
(645,482 observations deleted)

.         
.         *Replace remaining missing values with actual missings
.         replace plh0004 = . if plh0004 < 0
(0 real changes made)

.         
.         *Keep only relevant variables
.         keep pid syear pgmonth plh0004 kidsex01 kidgeb01 kidmon01 sex gebjahr
>  gebmonat

.         
.         *Dropping observations who have not already given birth to their baby
>  at the time of the survey
.         drop if syear < kidgeb01
(1,237 observations deleted)

.         drop if (pgmonth < kidmon01 & syear == kidgeb01 & kidmon01 > 0 & !mis
> sing(kidmon01)) 
(256 observations deleted)

.         *Kids with unknown birth months but born in the same year as the surv
> ey are assumed to be already born and zero years old
.         
.         *Dropping if year of child birth is not reported
.         drop if kidgeb01 < 0
(21 observations deleted)

. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         *Obtain summary statistics on scale
.         qui sum plh0004

.         
.         *Generate standardized outcome
.         gen political_leaning_respondent = (plh0004 - r(mean))/r(sd)

.         
.         *Code first-child-daughter dummy
.         gen first_child_daughter = (kidsex01 == 2)

.         
.         *Code age of child in years
.         gen surveymonth = ym(syear, pgmonth)

.         gen childbirthmonth = ym(kidgeb01, kidmon01)
(5,802 missing values generated)

.         gen age_of_child = floor((surveymonth - childbirthmonth)/12)
(5,802 missing values generated)

.         replace age_of_child = syear - kidgeb01 if missing(age_of_child)
(5,802 real changes made)

.         
.         *Code age of respondent in years
.         gen respondentbirthmonth = ym(gebjahr, gebmonat)
(150 missing values generated)

.         gen age_respondent = floor((surveymonth - respondentbirthmonth)/12)
(150 missing values generated)

.         
.         *Generate respondent gender
.         gen gender_respondent = (sex == 2)

.         
.         *Rename survey year and personal ID
.         rename syear year

.         rename pid respondent_ID

.         
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         *Testing the code we pre-registered, it appears that the margins() co
> mmand does not evaluate the average marginal effect of first_child_daughter o
> n standard_attitude_respondent. We suspect that this is because we only have 
> 5% of the dataset at the moment, and treating child age as a factor variable 
> when interacting with first_child_daughter could be yielding a sparsity issue
> , where not enough children are observed with the same age but different gend
> ers. This could potentially be remedied with the receipt of the full data. We
>  thus implement a conditional strategy: if the margins() average marginal eff
> ect evaluates, then we will use that average marginal effect, as it comes fro
> m the model we pre-registered. If it does not evaluate, then we will change c
> hild age from being treated as a factor variable to being treated as a contin
> uous variable. Our testing implies that this parameterization will yield a de
> fined average marginal effect estimate 
.         
.         *Original pre-registered model
.         reg  political_leaning_respondent i.first_child_daughter##i.age_of_ch
> ild i.gender_respondent i.age_respondent i.year, vce(cluster respondent_ID)
